        "body": "> **Status: product/write-action hold. Do not merge.** Rebased, conflict-free implementation and exact-head local proof are complete. CI was approved and is running; the owner decision below remains unresolved.\n\n## Owner decision requested\n\n**Decision:** Should CodexBar spend a finite provider-side Codex reset credit through an authenticated `POST`, or remain read-only and limit this work to reset inventory/expiry notifications?\n\n**Tradeoff:** One-click consumption is convenient, confirms before spending, refreshes afterward, and scopes authentication to the selected account. It remains an irreversible provider-side write through a private endpoint contract; confirmation does not remove endpoint-stability, authorization, or accidental-spend risk.\n\n**Recommendation:** **Do not land the consume action yet.** Keep CodexBar read-only until the provider contract is documented or explicitly approved. If immediate progress is desired, split and land the read-only inventory/notification work; retain this branch as the reviewed write-action option.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Builds on #1638: displays the reset bank and adds a confirmed action to use one from CodexBar.\n- Routes fetch/use through the selected Codex account context, including every visible stacked account.\n- Filters expired cached credits at presentation and action time, so stale snapshots cannot enable an unusable reset.\n- Preserves reset-only snapshots in menu-card/stacked layouts; avoids empty padded usage cards.\n- Includes the missing Italian reset accessibility localization.\n\nAddresses #1502 only if the write action is accepted; the issue stays open while this PR is held.\n\n## Validation\n\n- exact head: `c248d0cce2acf07d36b042bc4c41c0b553aba427`\n- rebased onto current `origin/main`; contributor authorship preserved\n- focused reset-credit decoder: 5 tests passed\n- focused reset-credit menu card: 6 tests passed\n- focused scoped-account refresh: 3 tests passed\n- complete `make te